{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1765457,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":null,"paid":0,"title":"Circuit hunt","festival_id":null,"organization_id":652294,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-03T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-15T13:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/circuit-hunt-shaheed-rajguru-college-of-applied-sciences-for-women-delhi-university-1765457","region":"offline","details":"<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 [&amp;&gt;div:has([data-free-thinking-preview-answer=true])+:is(.text-message,.relative:has(&gt;.text-message))]:-mt-2 grow\">\n<div class=\"TzNmiG_container gap-4 [&amp;&gt;div:has([data-free-thinking-preview-answer=true])+:is(.text-message,.relative:has(&gt;.text-message))]:-mt-2\" data-streaming-response-group=\"\">\n<div class=\"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1\" dir=\"auto\" data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"4717166c-6925-45a4-9a01-b1c15eb781c4\" data-message-model-slug=\"gpt-5-6\">\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden\">\n<div class=\"LR5Y_W_content markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full light markdown-new-styling\">\n<p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"786\" data-end=\"804\"><strong data-start=\"786\" data-end=\"804\">Circuit Hunt <\/strong><\/p>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"809\" data-end=\"1031\"><strong data-start=\"809\" data-end=\"828\">About the Event<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"809\" data-end=\"1031\">Circuit Hunt is a hands-on electronics competition designed to test participants' practical knowledge of electronic circuits, troubleshooting skills, problem-solving ability, accuracy, and teamwork.<\/li>\n<li dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"809\" data-end=\"1031\">Participants will compete in teams of 2 and take part in practical circuit-based challenges involving troubleshooting a faulty circuit and building a functional circuit using the components provided by the organizers.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"1258\" data-end=\"1274\"><strong data-start=\"1258\" data-end=\"1274\">Event Format<\/strong><\/p>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"1279\" data-end=\"1525\"><strong data-start=\"1279\" data-end=\"1320\">Round 1 &ndash; Faulty Circuit Challenge<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"1279\" data-end=\"1525\">Teams will be provided with a faulty electronic circuit. Participants must inspect the circuit, identify the fault, troubleshoot the connections, and make the circuit functional within the given time.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"1530\" data-end=\"1729\"><strong data-start=\"1530\" data-end=\"1563\">Round 2 &ndash; Build the Circuit<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams will be given a circuit requirement and the necessary components. Participants must design and build the required working circuit within the allotted time.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"1734\" data-end=\"1754\"><strong data-start=\"1734\" data-end=\"1754\">Judging Criteria<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-start=\"1757\" data-end=\"1991\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1eyvo4e\" data-start=\"1757\" data-end=\"1785\">Correctness of the circuit<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"ghlqgu\" data-start=\"1788\" data-end=\"1824\">Proper use of the given components<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"grok4w\" data-start=\"1827\" data-end=\"1850\">Circuit functionality<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"d5gx15\" data-start=\"1853\" data-end=\"1878\">Accuracy of connections<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"sjonvi\" data-start=\"1881\" data-end=\"1906\">Neatness of the circuit<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"10djc00\" data-start=\"1909\" data-end=\"1947\">Must complete the task within the time limit&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1xp7jyp\" data-start=\"1950\" data-end=\"1989\">Teamwork and troubleshooting approach<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"1994\" data-end=\"2011\"><strong data-start=\"1994\" data-end=\"2011\">General Rules<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-start=\"2014\" data-end=\"2548\">\n<li data-section-id=\"fccch8\" data-start=\"2014\" data-end=\"2052\">Each team must consist of 2 members.<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"79dhin\" data-start=\"2055\" data-end=\"2131\">Components required for the challenges will be provided by the organizers.<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"61z099\" data-start=\"2134\" data-end=\"2216\">Participants must use only the components provided for the respective challenge.<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"617lgx\" data-start=\"2219\" data-end=\"2281\">Teams must complete the challenges within the allotted time.<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1r3g1z7\" data-start=\"2284\" data-end=\"2346\">Participants must not interfere with another team's circuit.<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1l2n893\" data-start=\"2349\" data-end=\"2410\">Any form of unfair practice may result in disqualification.<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"u6vpuk\" data-start=\"2413\" data-end=\"2479\">Participants must handle all components and equipment carefully.<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"177te5o\" data-start=\"2482\" data-end=\"2546\">The decision of the judges\/organizing committee will be final.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"2551\" data-end=\"2575\"><strong data-start=\"2551\" data-end=\"2575\">Safety Guidelines \ufe0f<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li data-section-id=\"50jupa\" data-start=\"2578\" data-end=\"2628\">Follow all instructions given by the organizers.<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1ir50lr\" data-start=\"2631\" data-end=\"2704\">Switch off the power supply before making major changes to the circuit.<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"pe0gpp\" data-start=\"2707\" data-end=\"2761\">Do not intentionally short-circuit the power supply.<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"ob5fof\" data-start=\"2764\" data-end=\"2847\">Inform the organizers immediately if any component appears damaged or overheated.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong data-start=\"2852\" data-end=\"2867\">Eligibility<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The event is open to undergraduate students interested in electronics, electrical engineering, physics, computer science, and related technical fields.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"2852\" data-end=\"3021\">{Basic knowledge}<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"2852\" data-end=\"3021\">Op-Amp &amp; Analog Circuits<\/li>\n<li dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"2852\" data-end=\"3021\">Digital Electronics<\/li>\n<li dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"2852\" data-end=\"3021\">Circuit Analysis &amp; Troubleshooting<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"3026\" data-end=\"3097\"><strong data-start=\"3026\" data-end=\"3040\">Team Size:<\/strong> 2 Members<br data-start=\"3050\" data-end=\"3053\" \/><strong data-start=\"3055\" data-end=\"3064\">Mode:<\/strong> Offline<br data-start=\"3072\" data-end=\"3075\" \/><strong data-start=\"3077\" data-end=\"3090\">Duration:<\/strong> 1 Hour<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":33514429,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-03T22:55:58+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-04T15:49:39+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"AWEoCUB","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":0,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":null,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"show_reviews_only_user":1,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":10,"referral_leaderboard_show":0,"is_ad_free":0,"enable_gamify_leaderboard":0,"tpo_college_id":null,"publish_at":"2026-10-03 23:27:32","auto_shortlist_tri